.TH PASSKEYD 1 "October 2026" "linux-passkey 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
passkeyd \- Linux Passkey FIDO2 authenticator service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B passkeyd
[\fB\-v\fR] [\fB\-\-uhid\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-backend\fR \fBauto\fR|\fBkeyring\fR|\fBfile\fR] [\fB\-\-usb\-id\fR \fIVID:PID\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B passkeyd
turns the computer into a FIDO2 (CTAP 2.1) security key. It creates a virtual
USB HID device through
.I /dev/uhid
that web browsers use to create and use passkeys, and offers a D\-Bus service
(\fIio.github.haythmkenway.Passkey.Daemon\fR on the session bus) used by the
GNOME Shell extension and the Passkeys application.
.PP
It is normally started by the
.B linux\-passkey.service
systemd user unit at login and should not be run by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log debugging information.
.TP
.BI \-\-uhid " PATH"
Path of the uhid device (default \fI/dev/uhid\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-key\-backend " " auto | keyring | file
Where a new master key is stored. The default keeps it in the login keyring
when one is available. Once created, the recorded location is always used.
.TP
.BI \-\-usb\-id " VID:PID"
USB vendor and product ID (hexadecimal) reported by the virtual key.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/linux\-passkey/credentials.enc
Encrypted passkey metadata.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/linux\-passkey/key\-backend
Location of the master key.
.TP
.I ~/.config/linux\-passkey/config.json
Settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linux\-passkey (1),
.BR pkcheck (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
